# Frontend layering

`frontend/src/components/**` is the only production code that may touch the DOM
(`document`, `querySelector`, `classList`, `innerHTML`, `addEventListener` on
nodes, `createElement`, layout/scroll, canvas style/size/context). Other
`frontend/src` modules must go through those interfaces (`editArea.append(...)`,
`MediaEntry.setSrc(...)`, `csrfToken()`, and so on).

`frontend/src/entry/**` is the only production code that may talk to the
backend (`fetch`, `requestSaveEntry`, URL-encoded POST bodies, response
handling). Do not import `entry/make-request` from components, runtime, or
common helpers.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — DOM outside components
document.getElementById('btn-save')!.classList.add('btn-success');

// ✅ GOOD — component interface
saveButton.enable();

// ❌ BAD — fetch outside entry
await fetch(saveUrl(), { method: 'POST', body });

// ✅ GOOD — entry owns the request
requestSaveEntry({ content, name: dateSlug() }, { success, error });
```

Allowed exceptions: `frontend/tests/**` (fixtures may use the DOM directly);
`runtime/backend-variables.ts` and `runtime/externals.ts` (window globals, not
document queries); `rendering-3d/**` (WebGL on a canvas already obtained from a
component).
